// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`the daily digest (T627) > the fixture day, whole: counts, the feeds line, two short report blocks, three error entries, the failed run > fixture-day.html 1`] = `"<!doctype html><html><body style="margin:0;padding:16px;font-family:-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.45;color:#111827"><div style="max-width:680px"><h2 style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:18px">Daily digest — 3 items</h2><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:0 0 4px;background:#f3f4f6;border-radius:6px"><tr><td style="padding:6px 12px;font-size:15px"><b>In this digest</b>: 2 problem reports · 3 new error kinds</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:6px 12px;font-size:15px"><b>Feeds</b>: Gauge feed failing</td></tr></table><h3 style="margin:20px 0 6px;font-size:15px">Problem reports from the app: 2</h3><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%"><tr><td style="padding:8px 0;border-top:1px solid #e5e7eb"><b>Wrong rule: Vedder River (gnis:3062)</b><br>“The spring closure shows as open on Nov 9. The book says closed Nov 1 to Apr 30.”<br><span style="color:#6b7280;font-size:13px">Nov 9, 7:41 p.m. PT · looking at Mon, Nov 9 · map regs · app 0.5.0 (27) (staging) · android 35 · release r-0fa7927b16e5</span><br><span style="color:#6b7280;font-size:12px">Reply: allowed · id 5d1c0a9e77b3f210</span></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:8px 0;border-top:1px solid #e5e7eb"><b>App bug: Cowichan River (gnis:1392)</b><br>“I opened Conditions for the Cowichan and the flow chart was blank for about a minute, then it showed last week's line. After I pulled down to refresh it came back, but the level under it still said Nov 3. It happened twice tonight, both…”<br><span style="color:#6b7280;font-size:13px">Nov 9, 10:07 p.m. PT · looking at Today, Nov 9 · map flow · app 0.5.0 (27) (staging) · android 35 · release r-0fa7927b16e5</span><br><span style="color:#6b7280;font-size:12px">Not shown here: 32 more words, gauge, map position, install id. Full report: Review app → Reports (Sync). Reply: no email · id a41f6c2d9e0b7735</span></td></tr></table><div style="margin:16px 0 4px;font-weight:600">What to do</div><ol style="margin:0;padding-left:20px"><li style="margin:4px 0">Review app → Reports (Sync): each report in full, then fix or dismiss each.</li></ol><h3 style="margin:20px 0 6px;font-size:15px">New app errors: 3</h3><div style="margin:14px 0 4px;font-weight:600;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#374151">New</div><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%"><tr><td style="padding:8px 0;border-top:1px solid #e5e7eb"><b>TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'sid')</b><br><span style="color:#6b7280;font-size:13px">water screen · app 0.5.0+27, 0.5.0+26 · android 35 · 14 reports so far from 3 installs</span><br><span style="color:#6b7280;font-size:12px">first Nov 9, 3:14 p.m. PT · staging · release r-0fa7927b16e5 · id 3f9a1c7b2d5e8a40</span></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:8px 0;border-top:1px solid #e5e7eb"><b>RangeError: Invalid time value</b><br><span style="color:#6b7280;font-size:13px">conditions screen · app 0.5.0+27 · android 35 · 2 reports so far</span><br><span style="color:#6b7280;font-size:12px">first Nov 9, 3:14 p.m. PT · staging · release r-0fa7927b16e5 · id 77b0e2d4c6a81f39</span></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:8px 0;border-top:1px solid #e5e7eb"><b>ApplicationExitInfo: REASON_CRASH_NATIVE: signal 11 (SIGSEGV), code 1 (SEGV_MAPERR) in libmaplibre.so while the map was drawing the stream…</b><br><span style="color:#6b7280;font-size:13px">map screen · app 0.5.0+27 · android 35 · 1 report so far · the system ended the app · fatal</span><br><span style="color:#6b7280;font-size:12px">Message cut: 9 more words · first Nov 9, 9:02 p.m. PT · staging · release r-0fa7927b16e5 · id 0c4d8e1f2a3b5c6d</span></td></tr></table><div style="margin:16px 0 4px;font-weight:600">What to do</div><ol style="margin:0;padding-left:20px"><li style="margin:4px 0">Each error's stack and every report of it: GET /crashes (Bearer RUN_TOKEN). Fix or ignore each.</li></ol><h3 style="margin:20px 0 6px;font-size:15px">Gauge feed failing</h3><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%"><tr><td style="padding:8px 0;border-top:1px solid #e5e7eb"><b>Gauge feed</b><br>FAILED 2 run(s) in a row: Error: no station answered (asked 438)<br><span style="color:#6b7280;font-size:13px">was ok</span></td></tr></table><div style="margin:16px 0 4px;font-weight:600">What to do</div><ol style="margin:0;padding-left:20px"><li style="margin:4px 0">Open the feed status: https://bc-fishing-feeds-staging.horvath-dawson.workers.dev/status</li><li style="margin:4px 0">Read the run's error in the worker's logs:<br><code style="display:inline-block;margin-top:4px;padding:4px 6px;background:#f3f4f6;border-radius:4px;font-size:13px">npx --prefix app wrangler tail bc-fishing-feeds-staging</code></li></ol><hr style="border:0;border-top:1px solid #e5e7eb;margin:20px 0 8px"><p style="color:#6b7280;font-size:13px;margin:0">Feed status: <a href="https://bc-fishing-feeds-staging.horvath-dawson.workers.dev/status">https://bc-fishing-feeds-staging.horvath-dawson.workers.dev/status</a><br>Why you got this: Everything that is not urgent (HYDAT, roster drift, feed health) comes once a day, and only on a day with something to do.<br>Environment: <b>STAGING</b></p></div></body></html>"`;
